drirc: force_glsl_extensions_warn for ioquake3 and OpenArena

ioquake3's OpenGL 2 renderer with r_PreferOpenglES 1 starts every shader
with "#version 100" and "precision mediump sampler2DShadow;" but never
enables GL_EXT_shadow_samplers, so sampler2DShadow isn't a type in GLSL ES
1.00 and every shader fails with "default precision statements apply only
to float, int, and opaque types", on any driver.  The renderer gives up and
the game exits.  force_glsl_extensions_warn enables the extension with a
warning, and the shaders compile (mesa/tests/sgx_glsl_prec, "ioq3" case).

Debian's openarena runs /usr/lib/ioquake3/ioquake3; upstream builds are
named ioquake3.<arch> and openarena.<arch>.

--- a/src/util/00-mesa-defaults.conf
+++ b/src/util/00-mesa-defaults.conf
@@ -92,6 +92,17 @@
             <option name="allow_glsl_builtin_variable_redeclaration" value="true" />
         </application>
 
+        <!-- ioquake3's OpenGL 2 renderer with r_PreferOpenglES 1 (OpenArena on
+             Debian runs it) declares a default precision for sampler2DShadow
+             without enabling GL_EXT_shadow_samplers -->
+        <application name="ioquake3" executable_regexp="^ioquake3([.](x86_64|x86|i386|arm64|armv7l))?$">
+            <option name="force_glsl_extensions_warn" value="true" />
+        </application>
+
+        <application name="OpenArena" executable_regexp="^openarena([.](x86_64|x86|i386|arm64|armv7l))?$">
+            <option name="force_glsl_extensions_warn" value="true" />
+        </application>
+
         <application name="Doom 3: BFG" executable="Doom3BFG.exe">
             <option name="allow_glsl_builtin_variable_redeclaration" value="true" />
             <option name="force_glsl_extensions_warn" value="true" />
